    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "wh0sP",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 14957,
      "name": "90 · TEMPORARY NOTES",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": 64,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "KrNd4",
          "name": "Zone label",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
          "content": "90 · TEMPORARY NOTES",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-page-title",
          "fontWeight": "bold"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "YDVAl",
          "name": "Note",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1320,
          "content": "Placeholder data. The household is Ana Reis with one bank, in euro, and the bank names are real ones used as stand-ins. The country and the gateway are not settled: design.md records Enable Banking as the first adapter and GoCardless Bank Account Data as the second gateway the port is validated against on paper.",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "tUv4j",
          "name": "Note",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1320,
          "content": "This canvas was redrawn after Enable Banking's documentation was actually read. Three things on it exist because of what it said. Balances are read when a member arrives, because the roughly four-a-day cap applies to background fetching and not to a member sitting in front of the screen. Restoring access is a journey rather than a dead end, because consent is capped at 180 days for most banks and open banking has no renewal. The chooser exists because some banks let a member narrow accounts in their own consent screen and others hand over everything, so this is the only place the choice reliably exists.",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Rgzd7",
          "name": "Note",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1320,
          "content": "OPEN DECISION · Where do banks get managed? Question: Connect, Choose accounts, Restore and Disconnect all sit on Overview. With one bank that reads fine; with four, Overview becomes a management console instead of an answer to where the money is. Current assumption: they stay on Overview for this change. Settings gains a Banks page when the second bank is connected, or when anything else joins Settings, whichever comes first. What changes if the assumption is wrong: a Settings destination, one page, one route, and three controls move off the bank card. Nothing structural, which is why it can wait. The specs deliberately name no screen, so relocating is a UI change and not a contract change.",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hVm9n",
          "name": "Note",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1320,
          "content": "OPEN DECISION · Is there a stepper? Question: connecting is three wimm screens with a stage at the bank in the middle. Current assumption: no stepper. Screens with a Back read as screens, and a progress indicator for a flow that leaves the product and returns would have to represent the part that is not ours. What changes if the assumption is wrong: a Stepper organism is added to the library and the connect screens gain it.",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "KmXxV",
          "name": "Note",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1320,
          "content": "MISSING TOKEN · color-scrim. The disconnect dialog is drawn over a raw hex, because the library has no token for the wash behind a modal. It only surfaced when the dialog was drawn over the whole page instead of on its own plate. It belongs in the same task as the missing components.",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "RJ9pE",
          "name": "Note",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1320,
          "content": "The account rows on this canvas replace the Account selector's Balance text with a two-line stack, because an instance cannot be given a child. That is a stand-in for the component recorded under Components missing in canvas.md, not a pattern to copy into code.",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "QvAZO",
          "name": "Note",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1320,
          "content": "The library's Sidebar nav origin reports eight fill_container children sitting outside a flex layout every time it is instanced. Pre-existing, visible in 01-access too, and it does not appear to affect what renders. Recorded rather than fixed: the library is additive and this change did not set out to touch that component.",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "imports": {
    "ui": "../../../packages/ui/design/product-ui.lib.pen"
  },
  "fileToken": "3683336e-7c68-45c8-9b70-02662cde67b9"
}